{"chapter": "cotangent", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "08PV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$A \\to B$", "MATH_0002": "$A$", "MATH_0003": "$\\epsilon : P_\\bullet \\to B$", "MATH_0004": "$B$", "MATH_0005": "$A$", "MATH_0006": "$P_n$", "MATH_0007": "$\\epsilon$", "MATH_0008": "$P_\\bullet \\to B$", "MATH_0009": "$A$", "MATH_0010": "$P_n$", "MATH_0011": "$B$", "MATH_0012": "$\\epsilon : P_\\bullet \\to B$", "MATH_0013": "$B$", "MATH_0014": "$A$", "MATH_0015": "$\\epsilon : P_\\bullet \\to B$", "MATH_0016": "$\\epsilon : P_\\bullet \\to B$", "MATH_0017": "$P_\\bullet$", "MATH_0018": "$B$", "MATH_0019": "$A$", "MATH_0020": "$U_\\bullet$", "MATH_0021": "$\\mathcal{C}_{B/A}$", "MATH_0022": "$$\nL\\pi_!\\mathcal{F} = \\mathcal{F}(P_\\bullet)\n$$", "MATH_0023": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0024": "$B$", "MATH_0025": "$A$", "MATH_0026": "$$\nL_{B/A} = \\Omega_{P_\\bullet/A} \\otimes_{P_\\bullet, \\epsilon} B\n$$", "MATH_0027": "$D(B)$", "OWNARGEND_0001": "]\n\\label{remark-resolution}\n", "REF_0001": "\\ref{simplicial-lemma-trivial-kan-homotopy}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{simplicial-lemma-homotopy-equivalence}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{simplicial-lemma-qis-simplicial-abelian-groups}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{sites-cohomology-lemma-compute-by-cosimplicial-resolution}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-identify-pi-shriek}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{proposition-polynomial}", "REF_0007": "\\ref{lemma-pi-shriek-standard}", "REF_0008": "\\ref{proposition-polynomial}", "REF_0009": "\\ref{simplicial-section-standard}", "REF_0010": "\\ref{lemma-compute-cotangent-complex}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}[", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3e93ea06cf6b0998039bf087038d3dc9752034bd93e5fde96c8f13cafcd9802c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:559e6a006a444f6213b88d7349df55e8727e9ceb9a8e4b8346cdc11b0e3c6408", "source_text": "Resolutions<OWNARGEND_0001>Let <MATH_0001> be any ring map. Let us call an augmented simplicial <MATH_0002>-algebra\n<MATH_0003> a <TEXTITOPEN_0001>resolution of <MATH_0004> over <MATH_0005><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if\neach <MATH_0006> is a polynomial algebra and <MATH_0007> is a trivial Kan fibration\nof simplicial sets. If <MATH_0008> is an augmentation of a simplicial\n<MATH_0009>-algebra with each <MATH_0010> a polynomial algebra surjecting onto <MATH_0011>, then\nthe following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0012> is a resolution of <MATH_0013> over <MATH_0014>,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0015> is a quasi-isomorphism on\nassociated complexes,\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0016> induces a homotopy equivalence\nof simplicial sets.\n<STRUCT_0005>\nTo see this use Simplicial, Lemmas\n<REF_0001>,\n<REF_0002>, and\n<REF_0003>.\nA resolution <MATH_0017> of <MATH_0018> over <MATH_0019> gives a cosimplicial object\n<MATH_0020> of <MATH_0021> as in Cohomology on Sites, Lemma\n<REF_0004>\nand it follows that\n<MATH_0022>\nfunctorially in <MATH_0023>, see Lemma <REF_0005>.\nThe (formal part of the) proof of Proposition <REF_0006>\nshows that resolutions exist. We also have seen in the first proof of\nLemma <REF_0007> that the standard resolution of <MATH_0024>\nover <MATH_0025> is a resolution (so that this terminology doesn't lead to a conflict).\nHowever, the argument in the proof of Proposition <REF_0008>\nshows the existence of resolutions without appealing to the simplicial\ncomputations in Simplicial, Section <REF_0009>.\nMoreover, for <TEXTITOPEN_0002>any<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> choice of resolution we have a canonical isomorphism\n<MATH_0026>\nin <MATH_0027> by Lemma <REF_0010>. The freedom to\nchoose an arbitrary resolution can be quite useful.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2494a6e5226d6e5e6595bcf4f9cc9552b85155c734e9976ad4ecc834445f65cf", "unit_id": "tag:08QI:statement"}
